    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_48a9cc9c768a321ac06c322f491ad3d54281adc04c5375324c3c7ae00c597164",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Small uniform shifts act as resolving coordinates: they separate contributions before the unshifted limit coalesces them and permit later differential extraction. In long-polynomial fourth-moment calculations, zero-, one-, and two-swap residue families must be combined before cutoff-dependent terms cancel; in the multidimensional correlation formulation, the number of nonzero discrepancy variables selects the corresponding swap order.",
