    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4ab69ccdd4f289d5b4f7562d0c28738ed7e37c44abb158c73a53d3d79ecee243",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The unitary characteristic-polynomial model isolates the universal growth factor in a conjectural zeta moment. For a truncated characteristic polynomial in its stable range, the Haar moment is exactly a capacity-constrained nonnegative-matrix count, and Ehrhart dilation extracts a transportation-polytope volume as its leading scale. In the symplectic family, symmetry and even-diagonal constraints reduce the feasible coordinate geometry and change the polynomial degree.",
