      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Mollification and a Littlewood-type argument convert a zero-count problem into the logarithm of a mollified mean square. An imported differential-polynomial mean-square theorem then compresses the analytic input into a functional of test polynomials, and a hyperbolic-sine trial profile with a balancing parameter supplies an explicit upper certificate for that functional.",
