    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_812926586b97f8950b7007c264ac0d610f5a4897d18b82a70c209d40e3e1f3da",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The conjectural higher-zeta-moment constant separates a prime-local Euler factor from a residual geometric factor. Unitary characteristic-polynomial moments model the latter while visibly omitting the former; the hybrid Euler-Hadamard program restores both prime and zero data in one cutoff-dependent representation. The CFKRS moment polynomial is a distinct conjectural refinement that retains lower-order terms beyond the leading product.",
